# react-admin Development Rules

## Architecture

- Framework: react-admin v5 with simple REST data provider
- Auth: Custom authProvider with JWT
- Layout: Custom layout with persistent sidebar drawer

## Resource Patterns

### List Views
- Use `<List>` with `<Datagrid>` for tabular data
- Include pagination, search (via `<FilterButton>` or `<SearchInput>`)
- Add bulk actions where appropriate
- Use `<TextField>`, `<DateField>`, `<NumberField>`, `<FunctionField>` etc.
- Right-align numeric columns

### Edit/Create Views
- Use `<SimpleForm>` for single-section forms
- Use `<TabbedForm>` when form has 3+ logical sections
- Add validation with `validate` prop or custom validators
- Include `<Toolbar>` with save/delete actions

### Show Views
- Use `<SimpleShowLayout>` or `<TabbedShowLayout>`
- Format dates with locale-aware formatting

## Naming Conventions

- Resource components: `[Resource][Action].tsx` (e.g., `UserList.tsx`, `UserEdit.tsx`)
- Place in `src/resources/[resource-name]/` directory
- Export named components, use default export for the main view

## Data Provider

- REST endpoint base: configured in `dataProvider.ts`
- Follow REST conventions: GET /resource, GET /resource/:id, POST, PUT, DELETE
- Use `useDataProvider()` hook for custom data fetching

## Common Patterns

```tsx
// List with filters
const filters = [
  <SearchInput source="q" alwaysOn />,
  <SelectInput source="status" choices={STATUS_CHOICES} />,
];

// Custom row actions
<FunctionField render={(record) => (
  <Button onClick={() => handleAction(record)} />
)} />

// Conditional fields
<FunctionField render={(record) =>
  record.status === 'active'
    ? <Chip label="活跃" color="success" size="small" />
    : <Chip label="停用" color="default" size="small" />
} />
```

## Localization

- All labels in Chinese (Simplified)
- Use `options={{ label: '中文名称' }}` on Resource
- Date formatting: YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY年MM月DD日
- Currency: ¥ prefix with 2 decimal places

## Performance

- Use `<ReferenceField>` for foreign key lookups (handles caching)
- Avoid N+1 queries — use `<ReferenceArrayField>` for has-many relations
- Use `queryOptions={{ refetchInterval }}` sparingly
